#!/usr/bin/env harding
#
# BlockCannotReturn.hrd - BlockCannotReturn class.

BlockCannotReturn := Error derive
# BlockCannotReturn signals a non-local return whose home invocation has ended.
# A block's ^ transfers control to the particular invocation of the lexically
# enclosing method that created the block. Once that invocation has exited, the
# block may still be evaluated and its captured variables remain usable, but
# there is no longer an invocation to return from, so ^ reports this error.
# It specializes Error because the return cannot be honoured at all; unlike a
# resumable notification, no handler action can supply a meaningful result.
# Keep this distinct from the internal transfer used while the home invocation is
# still active: application handlers for Error must not intercept that transfer.
